<InfoPage
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  eyebrow="Commercial transparency"
  lede="Some Agewell Brief articles include optional links that can earn the publication a commission."
>
  <h2>How affiliate links work</h2>
  <p>If a reader follows an affiliate link and completes a qualifying purchase, Agewell Brief may receive a commission from the seller or affiliate network. The reader is not charged an additional fee because of that link.</p>

  <h2>How we label them</h2>
  <p>Affiliate placements carry an explicit disclosure and appear separately from the reporting. Our RSS feed excludes affiliate placements so publishers and feed readers receive the editorial brief without embedded promotion.</p>

  <h2>Our editorial line</h2>
  <p>Commercial availability does not turn a product claim into a health fact. Editorial selection begins with the news value and source material. We do not describe affiliate offers as independent research, and we do not hide promotional destinations behind editorial links.</p>

  <p>Questions about a specific placement can be sent through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</InfoPage>
